{"id": "EUVD-2026-76506", "enisaUuid": "326757eb-3b77-352e-9cbb-be75b974b944", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nhsi: omap_ssi_core: fix missing DMA mask setup for SSI controller device\n\nThe OMAP SSI driver uses a synthetic HSI controller device allocated via\nhsi_alloc_controller(), which does not go through the normal OF/platform\ndevice initialization path.\n\nAs a result, the embedded struct device does not have a DMA mask\ninitialized by default.\n\nAfter recent DMA API hardening changes, dma_map_sg() and related helpers\nnow require a valid dma_mask to be present, otherwise the driver may\ncrash or trigger warnings when attempting DMA mapping operations.\n\nFix this by explicitly initializing the DMA mask for the SSI controller\ndevice and setting a 32-bit DMA mask, which matches the hardware\ncapabilities.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:44:57", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:49:26", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6a5426f56de98faf7886702f8720828bf346a48f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a4beb841f84e0e6ad5ff3d114f43ad30165572dd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9ecef057b7a7f165ce66eaf07cb4cf85d10ed9c7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9963a65be2befff82b5f5a7cfcd7ac4aca081c0b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e8d47e309c704df95816e7442f05947424d8b33f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4e019e5e247bfe877fdf288f2d6ec1b4c850c7c6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fbffbfdae55954213fea99c5c9856c48dc705019", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e81250ec6b69248b00d38c523dc6a13efaf38aab"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89594", "GHSA-2c7x-rwh5-mhqm"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "029e48d3-d451-3919-b7e5-63fd5ea6030d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f959dcd6ddfd29235030e8026471ac1b022ad2b0 <6a5426f56de98faf7886702f8720